WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:07.174
"Why Does Ozempic Stop Working for Weight Loss
and What Happens When You Quit?"

00:00:07.174 --> 00:00:10.244
People may not understand
the potential limitations

00:00:10.244 --> 00:00:14.314
of the new class of Ozempic-like
anti-obesity medications,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.651
especially given the wide hype
these drugs are receiving.

00:00:17.651 --> 00:00:20.287
For example, the drugs
don’t work for everybody,

00:00:20.287 --> 00:00:21.488
and even when they do,

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:24.258
weight loss stalls out
after a year.

00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:26.526
The drug insert included
in every package

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.862
of the high-dose Ozempic
used for weight loss

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.631
shows these graphs.

00:00:30.631 --> 00:00:33.267
Here’s weight loss
on high-dose semaglutide,

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.903
also known as Ozempic,
and sold as Wegovy,

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:37.704
versus placebo.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.373
As you can see,
after about a year,

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:41.074
weight loss stops,

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.944
even if you keep injecting
yourself with the drug.

00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:46.780
Is it because you’ve plateaued
at a normal weight?

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.415
Sadly, no.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:51.385
They started out obese,
and they ended up obese.

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:55.155
Why does the weight loss
stall out?

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:58.892
Because of what’s presumed
to be a near-exponential rise

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.727
in calorie intake,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.330
as the same amount of effort
to cut calories,

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.265
whether through willpower,
drugs, or surgery,

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.801
is met with
increasing resistance,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.605
as ongoing weight loss activates
your feedback-control circuit,

00:01:11.605 --> 00:01:13.840
stimulating your appetite.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.376
So, at first,
the massive GLP-1 activity

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.179
triggered by the drugs
lowers your appetite,

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.581
but as you lose weight,
your body fights back,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.784
ratcheting your appetite
back up;

00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:26.353
so, the same amount
of massive GLP-1 stimulation

00:01:26.353 --> 00:01:29.856
causes less
of an appetite suppression.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.359
Within 12 months,
this resistance,

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:35.095
together with the decreased
total energy expenditure

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.596
from being lighter,

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.300
matches the persistent effort
to cut calories,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.469
and with calories-in
matching calories-out,

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.671
weight loss plateaus.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.340
Here it is, graphically.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.175
The same thing happens

00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:51.178
whether you’re restricting
calories on a diet,

00:01:51.178 --> 00:01:54.982
injecting these fancy new
GLP-1 Ozempic-type drugs,

00:01:54.982 --> 00:01:59.119
or going under the knife
for bariatric surgery.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.088
Take high-dose Ozempic.

00:02:01.088 --> 00:02:03.924
After the three-month ramp up
in dose,

00:02:03.924 --> 00:02:07.427
people are eating nearly
a thousand fewer calories a day.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.196
No wonder they’re losing weight.

00:02:09.196 --> 00:02:11.365
But then, the body fights back,

00:02:11.365 --> 00:02:13.767
pushing against
the high GLP-1 signaling

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:16.169
and jacking their appetite
back up.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.771
Not all the way back up,

00:02:17.771 --> 00:02:20.007
because they’re still injecting
these drugs every week;

00:02:20.007 --> 00:02:24.077
so, they still appear to be
eating 400 fewer calories a day

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.879
than what they used to.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.448
So, if they’re eating less,

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.984
why aren’t they continuing
to lose weight?

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.854
Because they’re expending
400 fewer calories

00:02:33.854 --> 00:02:36.223
simply because they aren’t
dragging 30 extra pounds

00:02:36.223 --> 00:02:38.625
(13 kg) with them
wherever they go.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.228
What happens
if you stop the drug?

00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:44.431
In this study, everyone was
started on high-dose Ozempic

00:02:44.431 --> 00:02:47.367
for five months
and started to lose weight.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:51.038
Then, some were randomized
to be unknowingly switched

00:02:51.038 --> 00:02:53.407
to placebo injections.

00:02:53.407 --> 00:02:55.675
Those who continued
taking the drug,

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.412
continued to lose weight,
until the plateau.

00:02:58.412 --> 00:03:00.113
Whereas, those who switched
to placebo

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:04.551
started to regain all the weight
they had lost.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:07.554
It’s the same with tirzepatide,
sold as Zepbound.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.357
As soon as people
stop taking the drug,

00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:12.159
the weight starts coming back,

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:14.227
and any benefits
that had been achieved

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.263
start to evaporate.

00:03:16.263 --> 00:03:18.732
Check it out:
here you can see what happens

00:03:18.732 --> 00:03:20.233
when people stop
taking the drug

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.569
after being on it
for more than a year.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:25.272
The pounds pile back on,

00:03:25.272 --> 00:03:27.674
two thirds regained
within a year,

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:31.111
and here are some
of the evaporating benefits.

00:03:31.111 --> 00:03:33.647
Blood pressure came down
with the weight loss,

00:03:33.647 --> 00:03:35.515
but then climbed right back up

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:38.251
as if they never even took
the drug in the first place,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.287
and inflammation
and blood sugars

00:03:40.287 --> 00:03:42.289
start creeping back up too.

00:03:42.289 --> 00:03:44.291
So, not only
does weight loss stop

00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:45.659
as soon as you go off the drug,

00:03:45.659 --> 00:03:49.696
but the weight you had lost
before comes back.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:53.100
So, like in this study,
you may have started out obese,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.301
and ended up obese,

00:03:54.301 --> 00:03:57.337
and to maintain your
less-but-still-obese status,

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.506
you have to keep
taking these drugs,

00:03:59.506 --> 00:04:02.809
presumably every day or week
for the rest of your life.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.578
So, these are forever drugs,

00:04:04.578 --> 00:04:07.114
the golden goose
for Big Pharma,

00:04:07.114 --> 00:04:09.116
drugs for lifestyle diseases

00:04:09.116 --> 00:04:10.784
that you may have
to take lifelong,

00:04:10.784 --> 00:04:13.253
since you aren’t treating
the underlying cause,

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.921
a fattening diet.

